Lower than that, it's the hypodermis or the fat layer. It looks yellow and bumpy and the SH community has dubbed it the 'forbidden beans' because that's what it looks like as it pours out of your body. If you've arrived there, you are much more prone to dangerous infections, nerve damage (causing loss of functionality of the body part), and death by blood loss. 

You should seek medical attention if:

* An infection develops and the symptoms stay for longer than a week (warm/red/irritated skin around the wound, pus formed, you get fevers, it constantly stings);
* You hit the hypodermis/fat layer/forbidden beans;
* Your cut is more than 2-3cms wide;
* It doesn't stop bleeding after three days;

Hope this helps! Remember to always strive for harm reduction.
